1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,176
My heart stopped beating three days ago, yet here I am, standing on a freezing train platform totally alive.

2
00:00:07,476 --> 00:00:14,364
Nobody notices the silence inside my chest, but everyone keeps looking at my wrist as if it's bleeding.

3
00:00:14,664 --> 00:00:21,864
I finally look down and see a faint digital counter glowing red beneath my skin, rapidly ticking toward zero.

4
00:00:22,164 --> 00:00:30,060
Panic sets in when a tall conductor grabs my shoulder, shouting that un-synced citizens must report for immediate disposal.

5
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:37,248
I break free and sprint down the foggy platform, cold air burning in lungs that do not actually need oxygen.

6
00:00:37,548 --> 00:00:45,132
Hiding inside an empty train car, I slice open my glowing wrist with a sharp key to stop the countdown.

7
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:52,872
Instead of blood, copper wires and blue liquid pour out, revealing metallic gears spinning where my veins should be.

8
00:00:53,172 --> 00:01:00,348
A recorded human voice suddenly echoes from my inner speaker—my own real voice from a life I completely forgot.

9
00:01:00,648 --> 00:01:07,944
I was never a malfunctioned machine; I was a human mind uploaded to hide from the city's mandatory memory purge.

10
00:01:08,244 --> 00:01:16,476
The timer hits zero, my fake body freezes, and I realize my real heart never stopped beating at all.
